#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:5
#: 084d7b9b1a75484bb613499ae0fc0dd2
msgid "Telemetry Logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:7
#: 019d0cb7c19c4ad9b32c5de6aa92b5e9
msgid "Telemetry logs (also known as \"tlogs\") are recorded by the ground station when you connect ArduPilot to your computer via a :ref:`telemetry link <common-telemetry-landingpage>`. This topic explains how to configure and access tlogs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:12
#: 492ca42de6464c2cbb46bdb5013f43b4
msgid ":ref:`Dataflash logs <common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner>` collect similar information to tlogs (see :ref:`Diagnosing problems using Logs <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs>` for more information)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:16
#: 42fd50a49b214e98a21639b954a4e62e
msgid "When and where tlogs are created"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:18
#: b5aa08faa3144b139d7d6186f6d99df7
msgid "Tlogs are recordings of the MAVLink telemetry messages sent between the autopilot and the ground station and are automatically created the moment you press the connect button on the ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:22
#: 75c27961010744b489782dd496088e95
msgid "If using the Mission Planner, files of the format YYYY-MM-DD hh-mm-ss.tlog appear in the \"logs\" subfolder in your Mission Planner installation folder or to the location you select in the Planner options [Config/Tuning] [Planner]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:27
#: 1d641c042f984888b52363e61090e4b8
msgid "Besides the \".tlog\" files, \".rlog\" files are also created.  These contain all the .tlog data plus additional debug output from the mission planner.  but cannot be parsed or played back so they should be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:34
#: b4bff9a5eeb74ea0aa45ca95b106477d
msgid "Setting the datarate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:36
#: 4241f57215164d87a29e098669da10cd
msgid "The desired rate at which data is sent from the autopilot to the ground station can be controlled through the mission planner's Config/Tuning > Planner screen's Telemetry drop-downs.  Because all data sent over the telemetry link is also recorded in the tlog, this also controls the rate of data saved to the tlogs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:38
#: 44757f2dcf6745e68f13df5aae7ade5c
msgid "Note that due to bandwidth limitations, the actual rate of the data sent and saved may be lower than the rate requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:44
#: 84628b2e553b4ba7be212aff170416c6
msgid "Playing back missions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:46
#: 3711a908fe8446b5830860a5fe4d682e
msgid "It is possible to play back a tlog by doing the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:48
#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:77
#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:129
#: 184eeccc536e44be9c4eed03d9d4fecf
#: 56172b97d7bd417f9f30995bf80e9a4a
#: bf4a0a4d1f4542548b2c4478d3032a62
msgid "Open the mission planner's Flight Data screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:49
#: 99f0f7430f6e4980a3ac47794756767f
msgid "click on the Telemetry Logs tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:50
#: ef81f1ab19b348a4a9215fe20da021bb
msgid "Press \"Load Log\" and find the flight's tlog file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:51
#: beea8963b2ea48de93e67842258f9fdf
msgid "Press \"Play\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:56
#: 022bb12921d74bcf82ea415914c16d9e
msgid "You can also jump to the point of interest in the log using the slider and control the speed of the playback with the predefined Speed buttons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:59
#: 68ed042f8b6b4934bf90985b275174fd
msgid "While the log is replaying, the HUD will move and the vehicles location on the map will update as it did during the flight.  Individual data values can be seen through the Status tab and you can even display them in a graph by clicking on the \"Tuning\" checkbox under the map and then double clicking on the data legend to bring up a box from which you can choose exactly which data fields are graphed as shown below.  This will show the recorded data changing as the flight progresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:73
#: e7a1319fa2a941e4bffb0e7ac2d58552
msgid "Creating 3d images of the flight path"
msgstr ""

