#: c19233a26fd649229a09f6509744bb1a
msgid "You can create KMZ files by doing this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:78
#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:130
#: 3615f458b9f34b1986b4c475524666e4
#: 203212019a7e421ba8a09d462e5e295f
msgid "Click on the Telemetry Logs tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:79
#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:131
#: 7cfa2b0ebda742a0abda75be389e768f
#: 10712cc64f8e4d93a34270760475ff3b
msgid "Press the \"Tlog > Kml or Graph\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:80
#: 1e85175dc04b4840a351b6dea9af69c0
msgid "Press the \"Create KML + GPX\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:81
#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:133
#: 3536fedb877048adb4d5929fb6da2dcf
#: dc37b3482cf242fe93d8cd89af8968e5
msgid "select the flight tlog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:86
#: 543b510f68e0460a8c21967f51c2c146
msgid "A .kmz and .kml file will be created along side the original .tlog and this can be opened in google earth to interactively view the 3d flight path. You can open the kmz file in Google Earth to view the flight or path. Just double click the file or drag it and drop into Google Earth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:94
#: e2293898a2be43859dd56791e2703c12
msgid "The different flight modes used during the flight will appear as different colored tracks.  You can change some details about how the flight paths are displayed including their color and whether the paths extend to the ground by doing this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:99
#: 6c8a16b18b7a4519b08bdfdc391991ff
msgid "Find the log file’s name in the “Places” pane on the left.  It should appear in a “Temporary Places” folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:101
#: 8cbe792e791b4c31b89c84b19378f6d0
msgid "Right click on an individual path and select “Properties” to open the Edit Path window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:103
#: 2f9fe5f6d640429a81356d1323b89f15
msgid "The color can be changed on the “Style, Color” tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:104
#: 25d6c2f93f9b46fd963abafb38f0b027
msgid "The area below the path can be removed (added) on the “Altitude” tab by un-checking (checking) “Extend path to ground”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:108
#: d405e68adba945ed9f8ba48c8638dc71
msgid "Extracting parameters and Waypoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:110
#: 70920b5045ff41ffbbdebb79a1f491c7
msgid "You can extract the parameters and waypoints from the tlog by following the same steps as for creating the KML file except that at the last step select \"Extract Params\" or \"Extract WPs\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:114
#: ba1a10f07cf941bebb6a11a6294f69da
msgid "Extract Params will cause a .param file to be created along side the tlog.  This file is tab separated and contains a full list of parameters (in the same order as they appear in the eeprom) along with their values during the flight.  This can be opened in excel or a text editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:119
#: 19ba33bfd4464edf9aa8c8993801e9d4
msgid "Extract WPs will create one or more .txt files containing any missions uploaded to the autopilot.  These files can be opened in the Mission Planner by switching to the Flight Plan screen, right-mouse-button clicking on the map and selecting \"File Load/Save\", \"Load WP File\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:125
#: b24de651150545acbd91084cc8b9729f
msgid "Graphing data from a flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:127
#: e24b3b9c3fdf4962a2d50916b9779af7
msgid "Data from the flight can be graphed by doing the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:132
#: a55b50a2392a4fc593b9a83d2a217bfe
msgid "Press the \"Graph Log\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:138
#: 89587ef439274ac4867c39b795cea47d
msgid "When the \"Graph This\" screen appears, use the left or right mouse button to click on the checkboxes beside the items you wish to graph.  Note that the items are grouped into categories like \"RC_CHANNELS\" and \"RAW_IMU\" although it's still often difficult to find exactly the item you wish to graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:143
#: e351b96e51d14579b04cdbb8f9504219
msgid "If you use the left mouse button the scale for the item will appear on the left of the graph.  If you use the right mouse button it will appear on the right"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:146
#: 782620c67e35472c8380c40f6fe7dbf3
msgid "Click the checkbox multiple times to cycle through all the possible colours"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-telemetry-logs.rst:148
#: 2b6f9428ff6d45ba9f2b7837424f424b
msgid "Change the zoom of the graph with your mouse's middle wheel, by select an area of the graph with the left mouse button held down or by right-mouse-button clicking on the graph and selecting \"Set Scale To Default\""
msgstr ""

